{"files": [{"id": 3636168, "name": "yahoo_password_frequencies_corpus.tar.gz", "size": 133771, "is_link_only": false, "download_url": "https://ndownloader.figshare.com/files/3636168", "supplied_md5": "76a39a14f8d24255993ea3db6f4b2520", "computed_md5": "76a39a14f8d24255993ea3db6f4b2520", "mimetype": "application/gzip"}], "folder_structure": {}, "authors": [{"id": 1372785, "full_name": "Joseph Bonneau", "first_name": "Joseph", "last_name": "Bonneau", "is_active": true, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}], "custom_fields": [], "figshare_url": "https://figshare.com/articles/dataset/Yahoo_Password_Frequency_Corpus/2057937", "download_disabled": false, "description": "<div>This dataset includes sanitized password frequency lists collected from Yahoo in</div><div>May 2011.\u00a0</div><div><br></div><div>For details of the original collection experiment, please see:</div><div><br></div><div>Bonneau, Joseph. \"The science of guessing: analyzing an anonymized corpus of 70\u00a0</div><div>million passwords.\" IEEE Symposium on Security & Privacy, 2012.</div><div>http://www.jbonneau.com/doc/B12-IEEESP-analyzing_70M_anonymized_passwords.pdf</div><div><br></div><div>This data has been modified to preserve differential privacy. For details of</div><div>this modification, please see:</div><div><br></div><div>Jeremiah Blocki, Anupam Datta and Joseph Bonneau. \"Differentially Private\u00a0</div><div>Password Frequency Lists.\" Network & Distributed Systems Symposium (NDSS), 2016.</div><div>http://www.jbonneau.com/doc/BDB16-NDSS-pw_list_differential_privacy.pdf</div><div><br></div><div>Each of the 51 .txt files represents one subset of all users' passwords observed</div><div>during the experiment period. \"yahoo-all.txt\" includes all users; every other</div><div>file represents a strict subset of that group.</div><div><br></div><div>Each file is a series of lines of the format:</div><div><br></div><div>FREQUENCY #OBSERVATIONS</div><div>...</div><div><br></div><div>with FREQUENCY in descending order. For example, the file:</div><div><br></div><div>3 1</div><div>2 1</div><div>1 3</div><div><br></div><div>would represent a the frequency list (3, 2, 1, 1, 1), that is, one password</div><div>observed 3 times, one observed twice, and three separate passwords observed</div><div>once each.</div>", "funding": null, "funding_list": [], "version": 1, "status": "public", "size": 133771, "created_date": "2015-12-23T21:21:19Z", "modified_date": "2023-05-30T10:44:26Z", "is_public": true, "is_confidential": false, "is_metadata_record": false, "confidential_reason": "", "metadata_reason": "", "license": {"value": 2, "name": "CC0", "url": "https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/"}, "tags": ["password", "Computer security", "Software Engineering", "Computer Engineering", "Applied Computer Science", "Human Information Behaviour", "Computer System Security", "Computer-Human Interaction"], "keywords": ["password", "Computer security", "Software Engineering", "Computer Engineering", "Applied Computer Science", "Human Information Behaviour", "Computer System Security", "Computer-Human Interaction"], "categories": [{"id": 29203, "title": "Software engineering not elsewhere classified", "parent_id": 29176, "path": "/28798/29176/29203", "source_id": "461299", "taxonomy_id": 100}, {"id": 26494, "title": "Digital processor architectures", "parent_id": 26485, "path": "/26212/26485/26494", "source_id": "400903", "taxonomy_id": 100}, {"id": 29236, "title": "Other information and computing sciences not elsewhere classified", "parent_id": 29233, "path": "/28798/29233/29236", "source_id": "469999", "taxonomy_id": 100}, {"id": 28822, "title": "Applied computing not elsewhere classified", "parent_id": 28801, "path": "/28798/28801/28822", "source_id": "460199", "taxonomy_id": 100}, {"id": 29122, "title": "Human information behaviour", "parent_id": 29116, "path": "/28798/29116/29122", "source_id": "461002", "taxonomy_id": 100}, {"id": 28921, "title": "System and network sec